From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: The Open Video Tools contributors <noreply@ovt.dev>
Date: 2026-11-14
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] inspection: extend insp_mi_data and insp_frame_data

Exports the per-block mode info that analysis tools need and the stock
inspection data lacks, and fixes the transform type:

- insp_mi_data gains partition, angle_delta[2], filter_intra_mode, the
  interintra and compound (wedge, mask, comp_group_idx, compound_idx)
  fields, ref_mv_idx, skip_mode, seg_id_predicted, the local warp model
  (wm_type, wm_invalid, wm_params[6]), num_proj_ref,
  overlappable_neighbors, delta_lf_from_base, delta_lf[4], cdef_idx,
  inter_tx_size[16], palette_colors[3][8] and the coded motion vector
  differences mvd[2][2] with their mv_joint[2]. Fields that do not apply
  to a block read -1 (mvd: INSPECTION_MVD_NONE).
- The differences are not kept by the decoder: read_inter_block_mode_info()
  stores them in two new MB_MODE_INFO members under CONFIG_INSPECTION.
- insp_frame_data gains the frame's loop filter, delta LF, CDEF and global
  motion parameters and its loop restoration units.
- tx_type is now read for coded blocks; ifd_inspect() copied it only for
  skipped blocks and wrote 0 for every coded block (inverted condition).
  Skipped blocks read -1.
- examples/inspect gains one flag per new layer (-pt -ad -fi -ii -wg -drl
  -sm -sip -wm -npr -dlf -cdi -its -mvd -plc -lr) and -X for all of them;
  -A selects the same layers as before.

INSPECTION_EXT_VERSION in inspection.h tells users which fields exist.
Every change is under CONFIG_INSPECTION: the default build is unchanged.

Upstream-Status: Pending [to be submitted to aomedia-review.googlesource.com by OVT WI-2.160]
SPDX-FileCopyrightText: 2026 The Open Video Tools contributors
SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-2-Clause
Rationale: libaom's inspection API (av1/decoder/inspection.h) is the only interface to per-block
  decoder state, and it omits these fields; no public control reads MB_MODE_INFO.
